33
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:29,160
The larger our models

34
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:29,510
become,

35
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:30,380
the more electricity

36
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:30,830
and compute

37
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:31,560
they require,

38
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:32,560
and that cost just keeps

39
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,520
increasing.

40
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,330
Biological neurons are

41
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:34,990
incredibly energy

42
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:35,680
efficient compared

43
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:36,330
with conventional

44
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:37,120
computer hardware,

45
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,190
which is why researchers

46
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:38,820
are interested

47
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:39,850
in whether biological

48
00:00:39,850 --> 00:00:40,200
computing

49
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:41,000
could eventually

50
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:41,850
complement or even

51
00:00:41,850 --> 00:00:42,960
